Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:28:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 117/121] RS2d part 1: draft temperature scale, one-hot
 threshold and verify dump

Sharper draft proposals for sparse chain RS (flash-next-bench
specs/RS2D_DRAFT_SHARPEN_2026-10-01.md sections 1-4). Defaults keep RS2:
- SGLANG_RS_DRAFT_TEMP_SCALE (1.0): the draft proposal uses temperature x s.
- SGLANG_RS_DRAFT_ONEHOT_ABOVE (0.0): rows whose top probability reaches
  the threshold propose one-hot q at rank 0.
- SGLANG_RS_DUMP_DIR: post-verify CPU dumps of p, q and acceptance for the
  offline grid (TP = 1 only; measurement runs).
Any q that both draws and verifies keeps RS lossless.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
